  "body": "What happens (v0.26.0): \"Offline local (Ollama)\" defaults to `qwen2.5:14b`. On a machine without it, Send fails with \"localhost answered HTTP 404: model 'qwen2.5:14b' not found\". \"Local Q&A\" defaults to `llama3.2`. The cloud defaults are old model ids: `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`, `gpt-4.1`, `gemini-2.5-flash`.\n\nExpected: the Ollama presets default to an installed model that can call tools (read from Ollama's `/api/tags` and `/api/show`, the probe in `crates/app/src/ai/probe.rs`). With no such model, the status says how to get one (`ollama pull <model>`, link to ollama.com). Cloud defaults are current model ids, kept in one table with a test that fails when a default is listed as retired.\n\nDone means: with Ollama running and at least one tool-capable model installed, the Ollama provider works on first Send with no typing. Tests pin the default choice from a recorded `/api/tags` answer.\n\nUser validation (reporter, 2026-11-23): before this merges, the reporter (mkinney) hand-tests a build of the PR in the desktop app and confirms it is usable. The PR stays a draft until that confirmation is on the PR.\n",
